  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sanjay Shadija vs State Of Chhattisgarh on 21 August, 2024 Author: Narendra Kumar Vyas Bench: Narendra Kumar Vyas 1/3 2024:CGHC:31701 NAFR HIGH COURT OF CHHATTISGARH AT BILASPUR CRR No. 933 of 2024 Sanjay Shadija S/o Shri Keshoomal Shadija (Wrongly Mentioned As Keshmool Shadija) Aged About 45 Years Proprietor Sehat Brand Farman Flour (Pecked), M/s Bhawani Aata Chakki, Daldal Shivani, Mova, Raipur, District Raipur, Chhattisgarh. ... Applicant versus State Of Chhattisgarh Through The Food Safety Officer, Food And Cosmetics, Janjgir, District Janjgir-Champa, Chhattisgarh. ... Respondent For Applicant : Mr. Paras Mani Shriwas, Advocate For Respondent/State : Mr. Karan Bahrani, Panel Lawyer Hon'ble Shri Justice Narendra Kumar Vyas Order On Board 21.08.2024 1. Sanjay Shadija vs State Of Chhattisgarh on 21 August, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/168301296/ 1 3.",
    "facts": "The applicant has filed this present criminal revision under Section 438/442 of Bhartiya Nagrik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 being aggrieved with the order dated 23.07.2024 (Annexure P/1) passed by the learned Sessions Judge Janjgir, District - Janjgir-Champa (C.G.) in Criminal Appeal No. 26/2024 by which learned Sessions Judge has dismissed the appeal as not maintainable. 2. Learned Sessions Judge while dismissing the appeal has recorded its finding that as per Section 17 or 68 of the Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006, the appeal has to be preferred before the Food Safety and Standard Tribunal, as such, the appeal was not maintainable before it. As such also the appeal is not maintainable. It has been brought to the notice of this Court that a memorandum has been issued by Registrar General of this Court on 17.11.2017 appointing all the District and Sessions Judge of every Civil District Court as Presiding Officer of the Food Safety Appellate Tribunal.",
    "arguments": ""
  },
